and let's go! Just like with the small

00:00:59.460 --> 00:01:03.270
and the large kaleidoscopes, the small
and the large ninja star cubes are

00:01:03.270 --> 00:01:07.470
modular origami models so they're made
up of identical units. Except with the

00:01:07.470 --> 00:01:11.430
ninja star cubes, we're going to be using
12 (twelve) instead of 7 (seven) for this video

00:01:11.430 --> 00:01:15.360
I'm going to make twelve sheets out of
three different sheets of printer paper

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:19.830
to make the smaller one since I think it
is a little bit nicer as an ornament but

00:01:19.830 --> 00:01:22.890
if you want to make the larger one
you're just going to need 12 separate

00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:28.460
square sheets from the printer paper so
let's go ahead and make the 12 squares

00:01:33.590 --> 00:01:36.659
Now that we have 12 squares we're ready
to go

00:01:36.659 --> 00:01:40.320
Because all the units are made exactly
the same way, I'll go through with you

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:45.149
how to make either one or two and then
you can make the rest. We're going to

00:01:45.149 --> 00:01:48.689
start out with a piece of paper that has
a fold in it by taking the upper right

00:01:48.689 --> 00:01:52.860
corner and folding it down to the bottom
left corner and then making a sharp

00:01:52.860 --> 00:01:57.689
crease along that edge. Once we unfold
the paper we now have a valley fold

00:01:57.689 --> 00:02:01.469
going from the upper left to the bottom
right we're going to make it a mountain

00:02:01.469 --> 00:02:06.240
fold by flipping the paper over
diagonally like this so that it's a

00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:10.319
mountain fold, then we could take the
upper left corner and fold it down to

00:02:10.319 --> 00:02:13.680
the bottom right corner. Line up the two
corners

00:02:13.680 --> 00:02:19.650
and also the edges and then we can make
a crease in the upper left piece of the

00:02:19.650 --> 00:02:24.480
paper here on that edge. Once again, run
your fingernail against it and then we

00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:30.090
could unfold it you'll see we now have
an X in the paper and this fold here is

00:02:30.090 --> 00:02:34.290
a valley-fold while the one from the
upper left to the bottom right is a

00:02:34.290 --> 00:02:39.329
mountain fold now we could take the top
edge of the paper and fold it down to

00:02:39.329 --> 00:02:43.379
the bottom. Once again,
just line up the edges and then make a

00:02:43.379 --> 00:02:47.609
crease along the top I'm gonna run my
fingernail against it just to make sure

00:02:47.609 --> 00:02:51.689
that all the nice creases are sharp.
Unfold the paper and we're going to take

00:02:51.689 --> 00:02:56.310
the top and bottom edge and fold it
directly on to the middle line just like

00:02:56.310 --> 00:03:00.959
that once it's lined up with the middle. Then once again, just make a nice sharp

00:03:00.959 --> 00:03:05.129
crease on the top and do the same with
the bottom: fold it up meet the two edges

00:03:05.129 --> 00:03:10.379
together just like that and then we can
make a nice sharp crease on the bottom.

00:03:10.379 --> 00:03:14.069
Now, I'm going to take both of these
edges that are folded into the middle

00:03:14.069 --> 00:03:18.180
fold this one to the top and fold this
one to the bottom by folding these

00:03:18.180 --> 00:03:23.280
segments in half fold it up like this
line it up and then make a crease along

00:03:23.280 --> 00:03:28.139
the bottom there just like that run your
fingernail against it and then do the

00:03:28.139 --> 00:03:32.489
same with the bottom fold it down line
it up with the bottom and then make a

00:03:32.489 --> 00:03:37.169
nice sharp crease along that new fold so
now we should have a piece of paper that

00:03:37.169 --> 00:03:41.400
looks just like this I'm going to do
something that I call a "slide fold" and

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:45.720
I'm basically just going to take this
edge here and join it up with this

00:03:45.720 --> 00:03:51.019
middle line by sliding the paper down
just like that

00:03:51.019 --> 00:03:57.329
So, just lay it down on the table and
just bring that middle edge right down

00:03:57.329 --> 00:04:02.790
to the center line and once it's lined
up all the way across just make a nice

00:04:02.790 --> 00:04:08.269
sharp crease on the top. So you should
have something that looks just like this

00:04:08.269 --> 00:04:13.409
Do the same with the bottom: so just grab
it round off the paper a little bit just

00:04:13.409 --> 00:04:20.250
like that and bring it up to the middle
to join with that top edge. Once both of

00:04:20.250 --> 00:04:24.539
the edges are touching then you can just
make a crease on the bottom. So you

00:04:24.539 --> 00:04:31.790
should have a piece of paper that
just like this now. (Break time!) Now I'm going to take

00:04:31.790 --> 00:04:35.810
the upper right corner and I'm going to
fold it down to the bottom so that this

00:04:35.810 --> 00:04:40.940
right edge is on the bottom just like
that-- just round it off, line up the edges

00:04:40.940 --> 00:04:46.280
and then make a crease along this upper
right edge again just make sure the

00:04:46.280 --> 00:04:50.180
creases are nice and sharp by running
your fingernail against it now I'm going

00:04:50.180 --> 00:04:54.650
to do the same with this bottom edge: I'm
going to fold this left edge all the way

00:04:54.650 --> 00:04:59.500
to the top by taking the corner and
rounding it up just like this and

00:04:59.500 --> 00:05:05.810
aligning this edge with the top. Once the
